  <h1>AI, Alignment as Standpoint, and Exact Intelligence</h1>
  <p class="lead">Modern AI safety tries to bolt behavioral rules onto opaque statistical weights after training. Hyperactivity starts from the mathematical root: partial observation fixes a <em>fiber</em> of compatible worlds, rational action requires a proof over the entire fiber, and alignment is a local correctness property checked on the participant's own device — never a leash trained into a model.</p>

